part pit_3
  tally 2
  law
  note "PIT-3 · The tax scale. pit3_rate holds the scale's marginal rates, read by marginal(pit3_rate, base) (L §5.8); pit3_reducing is the yearly reducing amount. The tax is the scale less the reducing amount, never below 0 (.3, the households' defs)."
  note "v2 governs 2022 (advances paid 2022-01-01 – 2022-06-30, the PIT-4 v2 .4 comparison, and the tax for 2022 until v3 was published); v3, published 2022-06-14 and in force 2022-07-01 (enters), governs the tax for 2022 on and advances paid from 2022-07-01. Under a cut from 2022-06-14 the later-known v3 wins the year 2022 (L §4.6); an advance reads the wording in force on its payment day (PIT-4 .2) through the pin wording <payday> for [pit3_rate, pit3_reducing] (L §4.3)."

source pit_3 "Personal Income Tax Act, PIT-3 The tax scale (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input pit3_reducing: money DUK question "What is the yearly reducing amount (PIT-3 .2)?"

band pit3_rate(x: num DUK): num
  note "marginal rates of the scale (PIT-3 .1), by base"

version pit3_v1
  cite pit_3
  governs 2018-01-01..2021-12-31
  known 2017-09-01
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "PIT-3 v1, in force 2018-01-01 – 2021-12-31, published 2017-09-01; governs the tax for 2018–2021 and advances paid 2018-01-01 – 2021-12-31."
  pit3_rate: [0, 90000] = 0.18 "PIT-3 v1 .1: 18 % of the base up to 90 000.00 DUK"
  pit3_rate: (90000, inf) = 0.33 "PIT-3 v1 .1: 33 % of the part above 90 000.00 DUK"
  pit3_reducing = 1530.00 "PIT-3 v1 .2"

version pit3_v2
  cite pit_3
